Changelog: 28-11-2026 16:24:23

Release 0.2.0.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 15:54:35

Fixed. The run wrapper points shellcheck at core's gamelog.sh from the repository's root, so the shell check in CI reads it.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 15:48:05

Added. When the window opens without a controller, a desktop notification says so and asks to switch it on or press its PS button (owner, 28-11-2026). The app's log notes it as a warning.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 15:36:57

Added. The emulator log is now written by core's gamelog.sh, as in the other game managers, and names the board by its host name (owner, 28-11-2026).

Changelog: 28-11-2026 15:14:28

Added. Every line of the emulator log now has the time and a level: INFO, WARNING or ERROR (owner, 28-11-2026). What KytyPS5-Native prints gets its level from its words, and its own ERROR or WARNING in front goes. Before the start the log also names the board, the processor, the game with its title ID and version, and each controller. Each display is named as its EDID gives it, without its serial number. No controller is a WARNING. A game that ends by a signal other than a stop is an ERROR, another exit code than 0 a WARNING.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 15:05:55

Added. The emulator log says what each game ran with and how it ended (owner, 28-11-2026). Before the start it names the build, the session, the displays and the desktop's mode. It also gives the game's size, the memory left and the GPU helper's state. After the end it gives the exit code with its signal, the time the game ran and the memory left. It then copies what the system log has from that time on out-of-memory kills, GPU faults and core dumps. A start whose wrapper was killed with the game is reported at the next start. KytyPS5-Native's own window now writes to the emulator log too, with the screen size set in its Kyty.ini.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 13:22:41

Release 0.1.1.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 12:38:25

Fixed. The comments and texts that name an emulator manager use its new name, such as PS5 PCSX2 Manager (owner, 28-11-2026).

Changelog: 28-11-2026 12:01:34

Fixed. The app is called PS5 KytyPS5 Manager now, with the device's name in front (owner, 28-11-2026). The window, the menu entry, the run script's messages and the wiki use that name. The Steam collection keeps the tag KytyPS5 Manager, so the shortcuts already in Steam stay in one collection.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 11:08:46

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 00:26:08

Fixed. The app folder's .gitignore opens with its license line.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 00:10:28

Added. KytyPS5 Manager, a new app for PS5 games with the KytyPS5-Native emulator, built like shadPS4 Manager. It
installs the KytyPS5-Native release it was tried with, checked against its SHA-256. It reads the VRAM split, the GTT
limit and the three GPU driver options and sets them beside what the emulator asks. It changes none of them. It
finds the games in Games/PS5, reads each title from the game's param.json and adds the checked games to Steam. Start
game, Games Uninstall, Exit KytyPS5, KytyPS5 settings, Steam artwork and the log work as in shadPS4 Manager. The
emulator's GPU helper is an option behind its own pill, which asks first and then asks for your password. The run
wrapper starts the emulator from its own data folder, so the saves never sit in a build's folder. A version chooser
and a Settings tab are not in this version. KytyPS5-Native is written for the AMD BC-250. It is not tried on
PlayStation 5 hardware yet.
